---
const cards = [
  {
    title: 'Custody stays with the user',
    body:
      'The service holds no wallet and no balance. A session draws funds only from an allowance the client approves, executed by the contract through transfer_from.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Two signatures per settlement',
    body:
      'The client proposes the byte counters and the node confirms the same values. A mismatch fails on chain, so traffic can be neither invented nor underpaid.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Sessions expire safely',
    body:
      'Every session has a TTL. If either side disappears, it simply expires. An unconfirmed session never moves funds beyond network fees.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Pricing anyone can verify',
    body:
      'Rates and the 20% protocol fee live in contract storage, and changes emit events. The same values the UI shows are the values enforced on chain.',
  },
];
---

<section id="model" class="alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Settlement without a trusted middleman</h2>
    <p class="section-sub">
      The coordinator relays signed statements and indexes the directory. It cannot spend funds
      or rewrite counters — the contract is the only authority.
    </p>
    <div class="grid g3">
      {cards.map((c) => (
        <div class="card">
          <h3>{c.title}</h3>
          <p>{c.body}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
